{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471965-totem-merit-question","id":471965,"title":"totem merit question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-07T19:32:52-07:00","id":471965,"title":"totem merit question","content":"Just for clarity can a pack improve their totem by investing additional merit dots post totem creation? <br /> <br /> If yes can the original boon be re-bartered or only added to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T19:41:07-07:00","id":471988,"title":"","content":"Yes. You can improve a totem after character creation.<br /> <br /> As far as changing the ban, I'd say mostly you would just intensify or alter the effect with the same general theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T20:22:24-07:00","id":472014,"title":"","content":"Yes I would increase the bans strength but I mean the benefits the pack revives can that be renegotiated as improved or only added.onto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T20:51:46-07:00","id":472062,"title":"","content":"I would say that it is added onto if the pack keeps the same totem. Afterwards, if they chose to hunt a new totem, who knows what kind of relationship they can have with the new one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4990-de_k47","name":"De_K47","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T23:10:36-07:00","id":472256,"title":"","content":"Why would it be changed? Like, i can't think of a reason you'd want to do that unless the spirit changed so drastically that it doesn't make sense anymore. Like, if your spirit of Information gave the whole group a dot of Intelligence, but then you increased its strength with Totem merits... you could add it giving the whole group a dot in Computers as well as the the previous Intelligence, but I can't think of a reason it'd <i>stop</i> giving the previous benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T23:25:40-07:00","id":472271,"title":"","content":"I was personal thinking it would make more sense to only add onto the existing benefits but had to get an outside option on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T00:29:56-07:00","id":472343,"title":"","content":"I dunno. If you can't change it, the only benefits it'll ever gain after Pack creation are Skill Specialties and single Merit dots. If you ever want a Skill or Attribute for from your Totem, better spend a ton of your Merit dots at character creation on Totem, I guess...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T01:05:28-07:00","id":472350,"title":"","content":"If you only add to what already was in place when you pass certain thresholds I can see that definitely working and making sense.<br /> <br /> If you can renegotiate the specific benefits your totem gives to the pack that still fits the same theme when you pass a threshold of totem points if you so chose I can also see that as a viable narrative. <br /> <br /> Edit: also the task or quest required / requested by the totem in exchange for this change could be an interesting narrative. <br /> <br /> I more just want to see if the community leans to one side more than the other and why because I'm rather inexperienced with werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T07:56:48-07:00","id":472744,"title":"","content":"I'm for the renegotiation idea.<br /> Say at creation your pack has only a couple Uratha and no Wolf-Blooded, so you get the 1XP boon. You take a skill specialty with it.<br /> Eventually you get up to the 3XP boon, so you add a skill dot for that skill. Sure this is just adding, but it's generally a broadening of the benefit.<br /> Once your totem hits the bottom half of Rank 3, you get 5XP and turn that skill dot into an Attribute dot. Maybe Larceny or Stealth becomes Dexterity. Again, you're broadening the scope of the benefit, but still keeping with the theme.<br /> Overall, this seems like a situation where the Sanctity of Merits idea applies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:47:53-07:00","id":473032,"title":"","content":"Any opposition to the renegotiation requiring a kind of quest from the spirit? Task for the effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:52:11-07:00","id":473048,"title":"","content":"You'd have to ask your group about that. I, personally, will not be offended if you just say &quot;the growth of the spirit has caused his boon to mutate like X!&quot; in your game or if you make them go through some extra heroic and sybolic effort to make it happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":". 04-08-2015, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:54:39-07:00","id":473050,"title":"","content":"Oh ya I'd ask my group for feedback before I put any of this in place but I build my ideas better with discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T11:10:19-07:00","id":473070,"title":"","content":"Personally, I wouldn't make the characters do some special thing to cross the thresholds between ranks (or lower rank 3 to upper rank 3 as is the case with the 5xp/10xp divide). It's a big deal for the totem, but it pulled it off by getting enough support/feeding from the pack.<br /> Then again, in my Werewolf game, I am one of the players, so maybe this is just my lazy side talking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T11:10:19-07:00","id":473071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471965-totem-merit-question?p=473032#post473032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any opposition to the renegotiation requiring a kind of quest from the spirit? Task for the effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that idea. Any excuse for more plot hooks is good in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}